{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pkwbbrma6gvsv4xudnnucthefp35jryfwvpoze7eyqq6kht5yzhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration\nThe whole library in `c_src/` is small and self-contained:\n- `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` — globs `src/lib.c` into one shared lib\n- `c_src/include/lib.h` — `typedef int16_t mp3d_sample_t;` + `void synth_pair(mp3d_sample_t*, int, const float*)`. **No** namespace-renaming macros, so the linker symbol is plain `synth_pair`.\n- `c_src/src/lib.c` — `static int16_t mp3d_scale_pcm(float)` (internal) and `synth_pair` (exported)\n\n## Completion gate (symbol diff)\n| Library | `nm -D --defined-only` |\n|---|---|\n| C `libtranslated_rust.so` | `T synth_pair` |\n| Rust `libtranslated_rust.so` | `T synth_pair` |\n\n`comm -23` of the two lists is **empty** — every C export is present in the Rust `.so` (the only other dynamic entries in the Rust lib are the standard weak glibc/ITM stubs the linker always adds, not library API).\n\n## Files written (outside `c_src/`, which is unmodified)\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `panic = \"abort\"`\n- `src/lib.rs` — `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn synth_pair(*mut i16, c_int, *const f32)`\n\nFidelity details preserved:\n- Float accumulation order kept verbatim (each `+=` step rounds in `f32`), so PCM output is bit-identical.\n- Range checks in the original order; comparisons widened to `f64` exactly as C's implicit conversion against the `double` literals `32766.5` / `-32767.5`.\n- `(int16_t)(sample + .5f)` reproduced as truncate-to-`i32`-then-narrow (matches the C/x86-64 lowering, incl. NaN → 0).\n- `s -= (s < 0)` uses `wrapping_sub` to match C's promote/subtract/narrow, and `16 * nch` is computed in `i32` like the C index.\n\n## Independent verification\nBeyond compiling, I built a `dlopen` differential harness loading both `.so`s side by side: **264,679 cases, 0 mismatches** — random inputs at four magnitude regimes (incl. values forcing both `+32767`/`-32768` clamps), boundary constants `32766.5`/`-32767.5`, `±0.0`, denormals, `NaN`/`±Inf`/`±1e38`, `nch ∈ {1,2}`, plus a 64k-point fine sweep over the scaling path comparing the full PCM buffer with `memcmp`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_read_input_tokens":24378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":732,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a53edc1f-3ca6-420e-99f9-eba576d9dd90","uuid":"832359b9-1026-4581-b327-48c7e2566a1d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:32:04.106Z"}
